+/*
+ * The GPU SMMU (iommu@1f08000, qcom,msm-iommu-v2, secure-id 18), context bank 0 = gfx3d_user
+ * (non-secure, ASID 0) at 0x1f08000. The global registers belong to TrustZone; as mainline
+ * qcom_iommu.c we ask TZ to restore the block's secure configuration (SCM MP_RESTORE_SEC_CFG,
+ * device 18; ios-river does the same for msm8953's gpu_iommu), then program CB0 with our own
+ * stage-1 tables, io-pgtable ARM_32_LPAE_S1 style (ias 32, 4 KiB granule, non-coherent walk):
+ *   - HakiosGPU's buffers at [GPU_VA_BASE, GPU_VA_END), 4 KiB pages, any physical layout;
+ *   - the kernel's own ring and fence word get GPU addresses from the same allocator (g_ring_gpu,
+ *     g_fence_gpu), so nothing depends on where xnu's RAM is (it may start at 0x20000000).
+ * If TZ refuses, or the CP cannot start with translation on, CB0 is turned off again and the GPU
+ * stays in bypass (contiguous buffers, the pools). sweetsmmu=0 skips it.
+ */
